    {
      "heading": "Must, not might",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A flat tyre. A repair kit still wrapped. Dad's note says Saturday, question mark.",
          "write": "flat tyre · kit · \"Saturday?\""
        },
        {
          "say": "She rode over broken glass? It could be true. But where is the clue?",
          "write": "✗ could be true"
        },
        {
          "say": "Dad suggests fixing it on Saturday. The kit and the note force that.",
          "write": "✓ must be true"
        },
        {
          "say": "Pick the answer the passage forces you to believe.",
          "write": "Must, not might"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Small step, safe step",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The right inference stays close to the text.",
          "write": "smallest step"
        },
        {
          "say": "He sighed once. Does he hate it? That jumps too far.",
          "write": "✗ over-inferring"
        },
        {
          "say": "Smoke means fire. You read the smoke, and know the fire is there.",
          "write": "smoke → fire",
          "draw": {
